IMPORT prelude

-- Statutory Corporations (Contributions to Consolidated Fund) Act 1989 (Singapore) -- the whole Act: what counts as revenue,
-- expenditure and funds (s 2), the Minister's power to require a specified statutory corporation to pay its surplus and its
-- unneeded funds into the Consolidated Fund (s 3), the Minister's power to amend the Schedule by Gazette order (s 4), and the
-- Schedule of specified statutory corporations with the Acts under which each is established.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SCCCFA1989.txt. The deposit
-- says the revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December
-- 2021"; its page footer reads "Informal Consolidation - version in force from 1/7/2026". The latest amendment annotated in the text
-- is Act 17 of 2026 "wef 01/07/2026", which deleted Schedule item 49 (the deposit does not say what item 49 was). Other annotations
-- below the Schedule: Act 4 of 2025 (wef 1 April 2025), Act 36 of 2022 (wef 1 April 2023, deleting item 34), S 845/2022 (wef 30
-- October 2022), and Act 14 of 2022 (wef 1 August 2022, deleting item 5). The source metadata records the version as current at 1
-- October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0220 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The honest answer is: nothing directly. The Act is addressed to the Minister for Finance and to 49 statutory boards.
-- A person or business meets it only at one remove -- as someone who pays fees or levies to, or has money held by, a listed board
-- (the CPF Board, HDB, MAS, the Council for Estate Agencies, the professional councils): the Act lets the Minister take that board's
-- surplus and its unneeded reserves into the Consolidated Fund, but NOT moneys subject to a trust.
--
-- Not encoded: what "financial year" means for each board (the Act does not define it); which of a board's moneys are "subject to a
-- trust" (that depends on the establishing Act and the general law, not read); and the Constitution's Article 145.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the example rows. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT for public use. See NOTES.md.

§ `Statutory Corporations (Contributions to Consolidated Fund) Act 1989`

§§ `2 and the Schedule -- the specified statutory corporations`

-- s 2: "'specified statutory corporation' means any of the organisations, authorities or corporations specified in the Schedule."
-- The Schedule lists items 1 to 48 with 8A, 14A and 15A inserted; items 5, 34 and 49 are "[Deleted ...]". 49 bodies remain.
-- The last four members of Body below are NOT in the Schedule; they are here to test the negative and nothing is said about whether
-- they are statutory corporations.
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority`
    `Agency for Science, Technology and Research`
    `Board of Architects`
    `Building and Construction Authority`
    `Central Provident Fund Board`
    `Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore`
    `Civil Service College`
    `Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore`
    `Council for Estate Agencies`
    `Defence Science and Technology Agency`
    `Economic Development Board`
    `Energy Market Authority of Singapore`
    `Enterprise Singapore Board`
    `Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore`
    `Government Technology Agency`
    `Health Promotion Board`
    `Health Sciences Authority`
    `Home Team Science and Technology Agency`
    `Housing and Development Board`
    `Info-communications Media Development Authority`
    `Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `Intellectual Property Office of Singapore`
    `Jurong Town Corporation`
    `Land Surveyors Board`
    `Land Transport Authority of Singapore`
    `Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore`
    `Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `National Environment Agency`
    `National Parks Board`
    `Professional Engineers Board`
    `Public Transport Council`
    `Public Utilities Board`
    `Sentosa Development Corporation`
    `Singapore Academy of Law`
    `Singapore Dental Council`
    `Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board`
    `Singapore Food Agency`
    `Singapore Labour Foundation`
    `Singapore Land Authority`
    `Singapore Medical Council`
    `Singapore Nursing Board`
    `Singapore Pharmacy Council`
    `Singapore Sports Council`
    `Singapore Totalisator Board`
    `Singapore Tourism Board`
    `Skills and Workforce Development Agency`
    `Traditional Chinese Medicine Practitioners Board`
    `Urban Redevelopment Authority`
    `National Library Board`
    `People's Association`
    `Nanyang Technological University`
    `a private company`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a specified statutory corporation` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `National Library Board` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `People's Association` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Nanyang Technological University` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private company` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- The Schedule's second column, "Act under which established or constituted". Several boards sit under an Act named for the
-- profession or market they regulate, not for the board: the Council for Estate Agencies under the Estate Agents Act 2010, the
-- Competition and Consumer Commission under the Competition Act 2004, the Singapore Medical Council under the Medical Registration
-- Act 1997. The PDF table is column-shifted in places (items 23 and 35); rows were matched by order.
GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A STRING
`the Act under which it is established` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority` THEN "Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority Act 2004"
    WHEN `Agency for Science, Technology and Research` THEN "Agency for Science, Technology and Research Act 1990"
    WHEN `Board of Architects` THEN "Architects Act 1991"
    WHEN `Building and Construction Authority` THEN "Building and Construction Authority Act 1999"
    WHEN `Central Provident Fund Board` THEN "Central Provident Fund Act 1953"
    WHEN `Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore` THEN "Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore Act 2009"
    WHEN `Civil Service College` THEN "Civil Service College Act 2001"
    WHEN `Communicable Diseases Agency` THEN "Communicable Diseases Agency Act 2025"
    WHEN `Competition and Consumer Commission of Singapore` THEN "Competition Act 2004"
    WHEN `Council for Estate Agencies` THEN "Estate Agents Act 2010"
    WHEN `Defence Science and Technology Agency` THEN "Defence Science and Technology Agency Act 2000"
    WHEN `Economic Development Board` THEN "Economic Development Board Act 1961"
    WHEN `Energy Market Authority of Singapore` THEN "Energy Market Authority of Singapore Act 2001"
    WHEN `Enterprise Singapore Board` THEN "Enterprise Singapore Board Act 2018"
    WHEN `Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore` THEN "Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore Act 2022"
    WHEN `Government Technology Agency` THEN "Government Technology Agency Act 2016"
    WHEN `Health Promotion Board` THEN "Health Promotion Board Act 2001"
    WHEN `Health Sciences Authority` THEN "Health Sciences Authority Act 2001"
    WHEN `Home Team Science and Technology Agency` THEN "Home Team Science and Technology Agency Act 2019"
    WHEN `Housing and Development Board` THEN "Housing and Development Act 1959"
    WHEN `Info-communications Media Development Authority` THEN "Info-communications Media Development Authority Act 2016"
    WHEN `Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore` THEN "Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore Act 1992"
    WHEN `Intellectual Property Office of Singapore` THEN "Intellectual Property Office of Singapore Act 2001"
    WHEN `Jurong Town Corporation` THEN "Jurong Town Corporation Act 1968"
    WHEN `Land Surveyors Board` THEN "Land Surveyors Act 1991"
    WHEN `Land Transport Authority of Singapore` THEN "Land Transport Authority of Singapore Act 1995"
    WHEN `Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore` THEN "Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore Act 1996"
    WHEN `Monetary Authority of Singapore` THEN "Monetary Authority of Singapore Act 1970"
    WHEN `National Environment Agency` THEN "National Environment Agency Act 2002"
    WHEN `National Parks Board` THEN "National Parks Board Act 1996"
    WHEN `Professional Engineers Board` THEN "Professional Engineers Act 1991"
    WHEN `Public Transport Council` THEN "Public Transport Council Act 1987"
    WHEN `Public Utilities Board` THEN "Public Utilities Act 2001"
    WHEN `Sentosa Development Corporation` THEN "Sentosa Development Corporation Act 1972"
    WHEN `Singapore Academy of Law` THEN "Singapore Academy of Law Act 1988"
    WHEN `Singapore Dental Council` THEN "Dental Registration Act 1999"
    WHEN `Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board` THEN "Singapore Examinations and Assessment Board Act 2003"
    WHEN `Singapore Food Agency` THEN "Singapore Food Agency Act 2019"
    WHEN `Singapore Labour Foundation` THEN "Singapore Labour Foundation Act 1977"
    WHEN `Singapore Land Authority` THEN "Singapore Land Authority Act 2001"
    WHEN `Singapore Medical Council` THEN "Medical Registration Act 1997"
    WHEN `Singapore Nursing Board` THEN "Nurses and Midwives Act 1999"
    WHEN `Singapore Pharmacy Council` THEN "Pharmacists Registration Act 2007"
    WHEN `Singapore Sports Council` THEN "Singapore Sports Council Act 1973"
    WHEN `Singapore Totalisator Board` THEN "Singapore Totalisator Board Act 1987"
    WHEN `Singapore Tourism Board` THEN "Singapore Tourism Board Act 1963"
    WHEN `Skills and Workforce Development Agency` THEN "Skills and Workforce Development Agency Act 2026"
    WHEN `Traditional Chinese Medicine Practitioners Board` THEN "Traditional Chinese Medicine Practitioners Act 2000"
    WHEN `Urban Redevelopment Authority` THEN "Urban Redevelopment Authority Act 1989"
    OTHERWISE "not in the Schedule"

§§ `2 -- revenue, expenditure and funds`

-- s 2: "'revenue' includes all moneys received by or accruing to a specified statutory corporation other than moneys subject to a
-- trust"; "'expenditure' means all expenses PROPERLY incurred by a specified statutory corporation in performing its functions and
-- duties"; "'funds' includes all general and special funds and reserves under the control or management of a specified statutory
-- corporation, other than funds created for the accounting of moneys which are subject to a trust".
--
-- The trust exclusions are the only shield the Act gives to money a board holds for others. Whether a given board's holdings (for
-- example CPF members' balances) are "subject to a trust" is not decided here; the caller states it by splitting the figures.
DECLARE `Accounts for a financial year`
    HAS `moneys received or accruing, not on trust`     IS A NUMBER
        `moneys received subject to a trust`            IS A NUMBER
        `expenses properly incurred in its functions`   IS A NUMBER
        `other expenses`                                IS A NUMBER
        `funds and reserves, not for trust moneys`      IS A NUMBER
        `funds created to account for trust moneys`     IS A NUMBER
        `amount the Minister opines it requires`        IS A NUMBER

GIVEN acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`its revenue` MEANS acc's `moneys received or accruing, not on trust`

GIVEN acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`its expenditure` MEANS acc's `expenses properly incurred in its functions`

GIVEN acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`its funds` MEANS acc's `funds and reserves, not for trust moneys`

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the excess of` MEANS
    IF x GREATER THAN y THEN x MINUS y ELSE 0

§§ `3 -- the Minister may require payment into the Consolidated Fund`

-- s 3: "Despite the provisions of any written law specified in the Schedule, the Minister may, by written notice, require any specified
-- statutory corporation to pay into the Consolidated Fund within the period specified in the notice -- (a) the whole or part of the
-- excess of the revenue over the expenditure of that statutory corporation in any financial year; and (b) the whole or part of the
-- amount in the funds of that statutory corporation which, in the Minister's opinion, is not required for performing its functions
-- and duties." "Minister" means the Minister for Finance (s 2).
--
-- Where expenditure exceeds revenue there is no "excess" and limb (a) yields nothing; the encoding takes it as zero (an inference:
-- the Act does not speak of a deficit). Limb (b) turns on the Minister's opinion of what the board needs, which the caller supplies.
--
-- FORK. The year's surplus will usually also sit in the board's funds by the time a notice is given (an inference). The Act joins (a)
-- and (b) with "and" and says nothing about overlap. The encoding caps each limb separately and does NOT state a combined ceiling.
GIVEN acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be required under limb (a)` MEANS
    `the excess of` (`its revenue` acc) (`its expenditure` acc)

GIVEN acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be required under limb (b)` MEANS
    `the excess of` (`its funds` acc) (acc's `amount the Minister opines it requires`)

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body,
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the notice is from the Minister for Finance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the notice specifies a period` IS A BOOLEAN,
      acc IS AN `Accounts for a financial year`,
      `demanded under limb (a)` IS A NUMBER,
      `demanded under limb (b)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement is within s 3` IF
        `is a specified statutory corporation` `the body`
    AND `the notice is in writing`
    AND `the notice is from the Minister for Finance`
    AND `the notice specifies a period`
    AND `demanded under limb (a)` AT LEAST 0
    AND `demanded under limb (b)` AT LEAST 0
    AND `demanded under limb (a)` AT MOST `the most that may be required under limb (a)` acc
    AND `demanded under limb (b)` AT MOST `the most that may be required under limb (b)` acc

-- "Despite the provisions of any written law specified in the Schedule": s 3 overrides the board's own establishing Act (for example
-- a provision there about how its surplus or reserves are to be applied). It says nothing about written laws NOT in the Schedule; the
-- encoding returns FALSE for those, meaning only that s 3 gives no express override.
GIVEN `the conflicting provision is in a written law specified in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 expressly overrides the conflicting provision` IF
    `the conflicting provision is in a written law specified in the Schedule`

-- The board must pay "within the period specified in the notice". The Act creates NO offence and states NO consequence for not paying;
-- the encoding says only that the board is out of time.
GIVEN `the requirement is valid` IS A BOOLEAN, `the period has expired` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation has not complied in time` IF
    `the requirement is valid` AND `the period has expired` AND (NOT `paid in full`)

§§ `4 -- amending the Schedule`

-- s 4: "The Minister may, by order in the Gazette, amend the Schedule." No affirmative or negative resolution of Parliament is
-- mentioned, so the Minister can add a board to (or remove one from) the list on his own order.
GIVEN `made by the Minister for Finance` IS A BOOLEAN, `made by order` IS A BOOLEAN, `published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule is amended in the form s 4 provides` IF
    `made by the Minister for Finance` AND `made by order` AND `published in the Gazette`
